# PolySniffer Native — Forwarder Lock

Authoritative design: `documentation/architecture/POLYSNIFFER_NATIVE_FORWARDER.md`

## Rule

**Native mode** browses `/admin/polysniffer/sniff/<host>/native/...` through the forwarder so TrafficLog/HAR sees proxy traffic. **No green orchestration bar.**

**Passthrough mode** is where Native evidence meets product UI: green bar + Insert Orchestration / bind action path → consumer.

Do **not**:

- Launch Playwright / external Chromium as Native
- Point Native at `/pt/polysniff/` (passthrough-mode path with the bar)
- Put Insert Orchestration / consumer-bind controls on Native Live capture
- Use iframes as the default SPA embed

## Success metric

RICH unmodified HAR (cookies, headers, bodies, assets, redirects) while the user walks the normal app flow in the unified workspace UI.

## After enough HAR

Build/refine the app-specific handler (isolation rule). Passthrough + orchestration attach (webhook → consumer) come later. Production Slack events remain API-first mailbox; Native Slack proxy is discovery only.
